The table below shows waist measurement and weight for 8 people.

\begin{array}{c|cccccccc} \text{Waist (cm)} & 72 & 67 & 85 & 96 & 80 & 90 & 98 & 105 \\ \hline \text{Weight (kg)} & 58 & 50 & 72 & 85 & 70 & 79 & 82 & 84 \end{array}

Calculate the correlation coefficient $r$ correct to 3 decimal places and describe the strength of the relationship.

The waist/weight data is shown below.

\begin{array}{c|cccccccc} \text{Waist (cm)} & 72 & 67 & 85 & 96 & 80 & 90 & 98 & 105 \\ \hline \text{Weight (kg)} & 58 & 50 & 72 & 85 & 70 & 79 & 82 & 84 \end{array}

Find the equation of the least-squares regression line.
